From 11ff99ccade85c37c812677af938d3a2bac811f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 06:35:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix recurring Prettier and link-checker CI failures on push

Prettier: the workflow installed unpinned `prettier` and the liquid plugin,
ignoring package.json/package-lock.json, so CI formatting drifted from
local runs. Use `npm ci` to install the pinned versions, and format the
21 content files that failed the check (whitespace only; rendered HTML
is unchanged).

Broken links (source check): failures were mostly false positives.
- Relative image/PDF links (e.g. rdd.png) only resolve after Jekyll
  builds permalinks; they are already checked on the built site by
  broken-links-site.yml, so only check http(s) links here.
- Skip the upstream al-folio docs (FAQ/CUSTOMIZE/INSTALL/CONTRIBUTING),
  whose links point at anchors that no longer exist upstream.
- Accept 403/429 from publishers that block or rate-limit CI runners,
  and ignore hosts that refuse connections from GitHub runners.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013WR9BPeZnFAvbcevkDomW3
